cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "TAKTO ONE: a sensor-integrated, tendon-driven hand exoskeleton"
message: "If you use this project, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Juan Sebastian"
    family-names: "Molano Cortes"
    affiliation: "Hochschule Anhalt"
repository-code: "https://github.com/molanocortes/takto-one"
abstract: >-
  TAKTO ONE is an open hardware and software platform for a tendon-driven wearable
  hand exoskeleton. It integrates twelve AS5600 magnetic joint encoders, two BNO085
  IMUs, a Teensy 4.1 controller that owns a Dynamixel motor bus through a 74HC241
  half-duplex interface, two custom PCBs, and browser-based operator and public
  consoles with a live 3D digital twin. The control law runs on the device itself,
  and motion capture is written to the controller's own SD card.
keywords:
  - robotics
  - exoskeleton
  - wearable robotics
  - hand rehabilitation
  - tendon-driven
  - open hardware
  - embedded systems
